ft lists are  migrants from the Indian state of West  Bengal the nationalist BJP government  insists this is a way to oust illegal  Bangladeshi immigrants not genuine and  in this way we need the NRC because many  illegal Bangladeshi intruders have  entered Assam as a result the rights and  identities of the indigenous people of  Assam have been threatened caramel  vanilla though the stories on the ground  show otherwise for many people here and  uphill battle is only just beginning for  those left off of the final list of  citizens this may well be the last  resort foreigner tribunals like this one  are being set up across the state to  feel the peace from those who have been  excluded and they hold the power to  reverse these exclusions people can  ultimately take their matter all the way  to the Supreme Court but such a lengthy  appeals process is challenging you can  get a good lawyer for this they need  resources they need money and as most of  the people belong to the lower strata of  the society for them it will be  Herculean task to gather that resources  and fight that legal battle in homes  across Assam there is only one thing  left to do  wait as the government finalizes the  names of those who deserve to be Indian  a core identity of millions hangs in the  balance  for more let's bring in DW correspondent  nimisha ties fall she travelled to  awesome a few days ago and met with  those most worried about the new NRC let  me show now  two million people have not been  included in that list what are their  biggest concerns for example might they  actually be forced to leave the country  well Michael for now a small amount of  good news for these two million people  is that the government has assured that  until all legal processes are exhausted  until all the appeals process as I  exhausted nobody would be declared a  foreigner nobody would be deported  nobody would be detained now these  people can appeal to water called  foreigner tribunals there are about